    {
      "title": "TEST PROCEDURE",
      "items": [
        {
          "type": "textarea",
          "key": "test_procedure",
          "label": "Test Procedure",
          "default": "The test procedure was in accordance with IEC 61000-4-8:2009 & EN 61000-4-8:2010.\n\nThe equipment was tested at the PFMF test site with a ground reference plane. The EUT was placed on a 0.5m wooden table which was in turn placed on the non-GRP. The test generator was bonded directly on to the GRP and connected to an Induction coil (1m x 1m) through a HV cable. The current and frequency of the source was set according to the requirement. The correction factor for the induction coil was compensated to achieve the required field strength. The AC current generated from the generator was given through the induction coil and power frequency magnetic field was generated through the coil. The test was repeated by changing the coil orientation in different axis. During the test performance of the EUT was monitored as per the criteria specified in standard."
        }
      ]
    },
